      "parents": [
        {
          "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/bitcoin/bitcoin/git/commits/be32083ddb17d5bc1667a56fe7f3b7a82f7e0e68",
          "sha": "be32083ddb17d5bc1667a56fe7f3b7a82f7e0e68",
          "html_url": "https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/commit/be32083ddb17d5bc1667a56fe7f3b7a82f7e0e68"
        }
      ],
      "message": "p2p: Don't apply ping timeout while downloading blocks\n\nIf the peer is also running bitcoin core, they will prioritize\nserving the blocks over answering pings. If this is slow due to\nour own download speed, we could timeout the peer even though\nthey did nothing wrong.\n\nTherefore suspend the check while downloading blocks.\nIf the peer is slow, we have other mechanisms (socket timeout,\nblock request timeout logic)\nto disconnect them, so the ping timeout wasn't necessary anyway.\n\nOnce the last new block is received, give the peer a grace period to send\nus the pong.",
      "committer": {
        "name": "Martin Zumsande",
        "email": "mzumsande@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-08-25T14:33:40Z"
      },
      "author": {
        "name": "Martin Zumsande",
        "email": "mzumsande@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-08-20T13:26:08Z"
      },
      "sha": "9e74c2f672c18c3818583326ef45f766a533d24c"
    },
